00:28:27,176 --> 00:28:27,892
investors.

859
00:28:28,072 --> 00:28:30,503
In fact, Buffett has written that his

860
00:28:30,503 --> 00:28:33,065
instructions for money left to his wife

861
00:28:33,065 --> 00:28:35,233
call for ninety percent in a very

862
00:28:35,233 --> 00:28:37,138
low cost S and P five hundred

863
00:28:37,138 --> 00:28:39,503
index fund, and ten percent in short

864
00:28:39,503 --> 00:28:40,948
term government bonds.

865
00:28:41,297 --> 00:28:42,191
Question one.

866
00:28:42,371 --> 00:28:44,078
Is an S and P five hundred

867
00:28:44,078 --> 00:28:45,587
fund enough on its own?

868
00:28:45,767 --> 00:28:47,950
Many investors use it as their core

869
00:28:47,950 --> 00:28:48,449
holding.

870
00:28:48,629 --> 00:28:51,141
Others prefer a total market fund for

871
00:28:51,141 --> 00:28:52,635
even broader coverage,

872
00:28:52,635 --> 00:28:56,234
plus international stocks for global diversification.

873
00:28:56,414 --> 00:28:58,306
Both approaches are reasonable.

874
00:28:58,486 --> 00:29:00,652
The key is low costs and broad

875
00:29:00,652 --> 00:29:01,807
diversification.

876
00:29:02,156 --> 00:29:03,108
Question two.

877
00:29:03,288 --> 00:29:04,798
Are index funds safe?

878
00:29:04,978 --> 00:29:07,443
They're diversified, but they still go up

879
00:29:07,443 --> 00:29:08,946
and down with the market,

880
00:29:08,946 --> 00:29:10,028
sometimes sharply.

881
00:29:10,208 --> 00:29:11,810
They're best for long term money.

882
00:29:11,990 --> 00:29:14,019
For money you need within a few

883
00:29:14,019 --> 00:29:16,897
years, safer options like high yield savings

884
00:29:16,897 --> 00:29:19,318
or short term bonds usually make more

885
00:29:19,318 --> 00:29:19,711
sense.

886
00:29:20,060 --> 00:29:21,105
Question three.

887
00:29:21,285 --> 00:29:22,786
How much money do I need to

888
00:29:22,786 --> 00:29:23,120
start?

889
00:29:23,300 --> 00:29:24,461
Often very little.

890
00:29:24,641 --> 00:29:27,544
Many brokerages have no account minimums and

891
00:29:27,544 --> 00:29:29,127
allow fractional shares,

892
00:29:29,127 --> 00:29:31,040
so you can start with a small

893
00:29:31,040 --> 00:29:31,502
amount.

894
00:29:31,682 --> 00:29:34,553
Some index mutual funds do have minimums,

895
00:29:34,553 --> 00:29:36,303
but ETFs typically don't.

896
00:29:36,652 --> 00:29:37,651
Question four.

897
00:29:37,831 --> 00:29:39,723
Isn't the market too high right now?

898
00:29:39,903 --> 00:29:42,477
People have asked that question at almost

899
00:29:42,477 --> 00:29:43,920
every point in history.

900
00:29:44,100 --> 00:29:47,235
Nobody can reliably predict short term moves.

901
00:29:47,415 --> 00:29:50,833
Regular automatic investing spreads your purchases over

902
00:29:50,833 --> 00:29:52,883
time, so you don't have to guess.

903
00:29:53,233 --> 00:29:54,174
Question five.

904
00:29:54,354 --> 00:29:56,711
What if everyone buys index funds?

905
00:29:56,891 --> 00:29:59,738
Some people worry that if everyone indexes,

906
00:29:59,738 --> 00:30:01,128
markets stop working.

907
00:30:01,308 --> 00:30:04,155
In reality, plenty of active traders and

908
00:30:04,155 --> 00:30:07,357
investors are still setting prices every day.

909
00:30:07,537 --> 00:30:09,657
It's a debate among economists,

910
00:30:09,657 --> 00:30:11,777
but for an individual investor,

911
00:30:11,777 --> 00:30:13,965
it's not a reason to avoid index

912
00:30:13,965 --> 00:30:14,375
funds.

913
00:30:14,725 --> 00:30:15,886
Question six.

914
00:30:16,066 --> 00:30:18,156
Should I pick individual stocks too?

915
00:30:18,336 --> 00:30:20,542
You can, but it's not necessary.

916
00:30:20,722 --> 00:30:23,996
Many successful investors own only index funds

917
00:30:23,996 --> 00:30:25,633
for their entire lives.

918
00:30:25,813 --> 00:30:27,551
If you enjoy picking stocks,

919
00:30:27,551 --> 00:30:29,227
keep it to a small share of

920
00:30:29,227 --> 00:30:31,648
your money, and be honest with yourself

921
00:30:31,648 --> 00:30:34,318
about whether it's beating your index funds

922
00:30:34,318 --> 00:30:34,939
over time.

923
00:30:35,288 --> 00:30:36,299
Question seven.

924
00:30:36,479 --> 00:30:39,079
What about international index funds?

925
00:30:39,259 --> 00:30:39,596
U.

926
00:30:39,776 --> 00:30:40,147
S.

927
00:30:40,327 --> 00:30:42,863
stocks have performed very well in recent

928
00:30:42,863 --> 00:30:45,399
decades, but there have been long periods

929
00:30:45,399 --> 00:30:47,688
when international stocks did better.

930
00:30:47,868 --> 00:30:51,310
Many investors hold some international index funds

931
00:30:51,310 --> 00:30:52,686
for diversification.

932
00:30:52,866 --> 00:30:55,771
Total world funds include both in one

933
00:30:55,771 --> 00:30:56,163
fund.

934
00:30:56,513 --> 00:30:57,407
Question eight.

935
00:30:57,587 --> 00:30:59,561
Do index funds pay dividends?

936
00:30:59,741 --> 00:31:00,182
Yes.

937
00:31:00,362 --> 00:31:03,163
Stock index funds collect dividends from the

938
00:31:03,163 --> 00:31:05,391
companies they own and pass them on

939
00:31:05,391 --> 00:31:07,874
to shareholders, usually every quarter.

940
00:31:08,054 --> 00:31:09,685
You can take them as cash or

941
00:31:09,685 --> 00:31:11,316
reinvest them automatically.

942
00:31:11,496 --> 00:31:12,791
For long term money,

943
00:31:12,791 --> 00:31:15,447
reinvesting is usually the better choice,

944
00:31:15,447 --> 00:31:18,296
because those dividends buy more shares that

945
00:31:18,296 --> 00:31:20,239
pay even more dividends later.

946
00:31:20,588 --> 00:31:21,494
Mistake one.

947
00:31:21,674 --> 00:31:23,752
Buying an expensive index fund.

948
00:31:23,932 --> 00:31:25,639
Not all index funds are cheap.

949
00:31:25,819 --> 00:31:27,922
Some charge far more than others for

950
00:31:27,922 --> 00:31:29,383
nearly the same holdings.

951
00:31:29,563 --> 00:31:32,663
Always compare expense ratios before buying.

952
00:31:32,843 --> 00:31:34,667
A fund tracking the S and P

953
00:31:34,667 --> 00:31:36,828
five hundred at half a percent a

954
00:31:36,828 --> 00:31:38,786
year is doing the same job as

955
00:31:38,786 --> 00:31:41,083
one charging a few hundredths of a

956
00:31:41,083 --> 00:31:43,717
percent, and you'd be paying many times

957
00:31:43,717 --> 00:31:44,527
more for it,

958
00:31:44,527 --> 00:31:46,148
every year, for decades.

959
00:31:46,498 --> 00:31:47,578
Mistake two.

960
00:31:47,758 --> 00:31:49,987
Owning too many overlapping funds.

961
00:31:50,167 --> 00:31:51,967
Five different large company U.

962
00:31:52,147 --> 00:31:52,484
S.

963
00:31:52,664 --> 00:31:55,229
funds often hold mostly the same stocks.

964
00:31:55,409 --> 00:31:59,066
That adds complexity without adding real diversification.

965
00:31:59,246 --> 00:32:01,234
It can also make your mix harder

966
00:32:01,234 --> 00:32:02,973
to understand and rebalance.

967
00:32:03,153 --> 00:32:05,280
Check the top holdings of each fund

968
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:05,766
you own.

969
00:32:05,946 --> 00:32:07,967
If they look nearly identical,

970
00:32:07,967 --> 00:32:09,719
you can probably simplify.

971
00:32:10,068 --> 00:32:11,020
Mistake three.

972
00:32:11,200 --> 00:32:13,348
Trading index funds like stocks.

973
00:32:13,528 --> 00:32:15,922
Buying and selling based on news defeats

974
00:32:15,922 --> 00:32:16,640
the purpose.

975
00:32:16,820 --> 00:32:18,991
The power comes from holding for years.

976
00:32:19,171 --> 00:32:21,412
Every trade is a chance to sell

977
00:32:21,412 --> 00:32:23,581
low, buy high and pay taxes in

978
00:32:23,581 --> 00:32:24,883
a taxable account.

979
00:32:25,063 --> 00:32:27,660
The best index investors often go months

980
00:32:27,660 --> 00:32:28,894
without logging in.

981
00:32:29,244 --> 00:32:30,301
Mistake four.

982
00:32:30,481 --> 00:32:33,325
Stopping contributions during a crash.

983
00:32:33,505 --> 00:32:35,601
That's when your monthly money buys the

984
00:32:35,601 --> 00:32:36,245
most shares.

985
00:32:36,425 --> 00:32:39,233
Many long term investors see crashes as

986
00:32:39,233 --> 00:32:39,665
sales.

987
00:32:39,845 --> 00:32:41,969
When the price of something you plan

988
00:32:41,969 --> 00:32:43,740
to own for thirty years drops,

989
00:32:43,740 --> 00:32:46,218
your monthly contribution buys more of it.

990
00:32:46,398 --> 00:32:48,764
Stopping right then means missing the cheapest

991
00:32:48,764 --> 00:32:49,998
shares you may ever get.

